# Run BOTH APIs first. Tokens come from the Identity API's real login (demo password: demo123).
# HMS checks them with Identity's public key from /.well-known/jwks.json (RS256).
@identity = http://localhost:5077
@hms = http://localhost:5041

### Health - should say Healthy
GET {{hms}}/health

### Receptionist DN10110 (Swetha)
# @name reception
POST {{identity}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "DN10110", "password": "demo123" }

### Any valid token -> 200 (proves HMS accepts Identity's RS256 token)
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{reception.response.body.accessToken}}

### Front Desk licensed + REGISTRATION_CREATE -> 200
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/front-desk
Authorization: Bearer {{reception.response.body.accessToken}}

### Admin-only permission -> 403 for a receptionist
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/all-collections
Authorization: Bearer {{reception.response.body.accessToken}}

### No token -> 401
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/whoami

### Tampered token -> 401 (last characters of the signature changed)
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{reception.response.body.accessToken}}xyz

### Admin PS10210 (Swetha)
# @name admin
POST {{identity}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "PS10210", "password": "demo123" }

### Admin -> 200
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/all-collections
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}
